      "worked_solution": "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t}+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
